    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0387" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.77/737: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-04T09:00:00+03:25">March 4, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Reference Department’s 71, February 10. British have submitted draft railway
                    financial agreement for consideration by Soviet Embassy and this office.
                    Substance of draft appears satisfactory to PGC and to me after careful study.
                    Text will be forwarded by air pouch leaving March 8.<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d383-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d383-f1" n="47" xml:id="d383-f1-content">
                <p>Text of draft agreement was transmitted to the Department in despatch 869, March
                    7, from Tehran.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
